    "sources": {
      "CH04": "reference/manifests/CH04.manifest.json + reference/manifests/CH04.dispositions.json (committed, gate-passed, hand-authored). map035/ev001/p1 is the arrival_nudge fingerprint's first verified instance, dispositioned beat:B8.",
      "CH05": "PLAYTEST_AUTHORING_IMPROVEMENT_V2.md §4b.5, a verbatim exhaustive hand worklist compiled 2026-08-27 covering Map036 (8 events/14 pages) and Map037 (8 events/9 pages). No CH05 manifest existed at authoring time (maps 36/37 may never have been staged through the transpiler) -- CH05 matches below are DERIVED FROM PROSE ONLY, not from real ManifestRow content, so their params (trigger, phone, rider, double) are best-effort inference from the described idiom shape, not verified byte-exact the way CH04's are."
    },
    "known_prose_arithmetic_note": "The §4b.5 worklist's stated page totals (Map036: 14, Map037: 9) do not cleanly reconcile against a literal per-bullet page count derived here (Map036 sums to 15 across ev1 cave-exit(1) + ev2 door/warp+nudge(2) + 4 trainer/item-ball-style events... ); left as-is rather than silently adjusted -- if CH05 is ever generated for real, the derived output is the tiebreaker, not this file.",
    "map037_staircases_caveat": "ev3/ev6/ev7/ev8 on Map037 are described in the source worklist as event pages, but the generator absorbed diagonal-stair events into `terrain` rows on 2026-09-01 (after the worklist was written). Expectation: these should NOT appear as `kind==\"page\"` rows in a freshly generated CH05 manifest at all. If they do, the generator's terrain-absorption regressed -- report loudly per task instructions.",
    "resolutions": [
      {
        "date": "2026-09-01",
        "what": "CH05 params adopted from the real derivation",
        "why": "CH05's maps 36/37 turned out to be staged, so a real manifest generated. The prose freeze could not know page triggers and honestly recorded them as null. Structure matched exactly; only the unknowable params differed. _header.known_prose_arithmetic_note already prescribed the derived output as tiebreaker in this case."
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-09-01",
        "what": "`rider` recomputed on both chapters after _RIDER_TAGS narrowed to {giveitem}",
        "why": "The frozen value came from a spec error, not from the source data: `rider` originally included `self_switch_write`, which every pbTrainerBattle page 0 writes to gate its re-talk page, making the param constant-True and non-discriminating. It now tracks the V2 census axis it was meant to: an item grant folded into the battle page."
      }
    ]
  },
